Yeah, mind flayers are really not that tough when you think about it.
They're fairly slow, have no ranged attacks, and don't wear armor
(IIRC). I recently did a genoless ascension and didn't get sucked
once.

NEVER melee a mind flayer. I learned this the hard way. No matter how
good an artifact weapon you have (or even a cockatrice corpse) this is
*not* something you want to do! Engrave Elbereth, zap a /oT (at the
mind flayer or at yourself), drop a scroll of scare monster, jump
away...anything to keep it two squares or more away from you. At that
distance it's completely harmless. Any closer and it's utterly deadly.
Oh, and wear a helmet, making sure to keep a layer of grease on it at
all times. And if you ever get the message about sensing psychic
energy, put on a blindfold *right away* and find out exactly where the
creature is (assuming you have telepathy.) Take it out with ranged
weapons (poisoned arrows work wonderfully for this purpose; mind
flayers are not poison-resistant, and it's often possible to kill them
in one shot.)

